# Build output
bin/
obj/

# The validation virtualenv: numpy, astropy, poppy, skyfield and galsim, several hundred
# megabytes of other people's code. tools/README.md says how to rebuild it in one command.
validation-env/

# The deep-sky maps. None of these are redistributable and every one is built on the user's own
# machine from the surveys; together they run to hundreds of megabytes. data/ITSELF is tracked,
# because the two small catalogues below live there.
data/*.starcat
# and the all-sky build's sidecars: proper motion, source ids, astrophysical parameters,
# 32 GB between them, which git should never be offered.
data/*.starcat.*
data/*.dustmap
data/*.emission
data/*.patchset
data/*.galcat
data/*.galimg
data/*.cache/
# The patch manifest describes whichever local patch files exist, so it is local too.
data/GaiaPatches.manifest
# The water-vapour transmission grid and the ESO tarball it is built from: 7 MB and 180 MB,
# somebody else's data, and rebuildable with tools/fetch_pwv_grid.py. Studio declares the term
# absent at /api/capture/data when the grid is not there, the same as it does for the sky maps.
data/PwvTransmission.grid
# Instruments the observer defined, written back so they survive a restart. Somebody's own
# telescope is their record and not this repository's: it names their site, their detector and
# often an unpublished QE curve. Rebuildable by POSTing it again, and exportable from the
# instrument panel when it IS meant to be shared.
data/CustomInstruments.json
data/CustomInstruments.json.tmp
data/pwv_R60k.tar.gz
# Bulk Gaia files, downloaded on demand and reused; gigabytes, and rebuildable.
tools/gaia_bulk_cache/
# The all sky build's scratch: per band buckets and in flight source files, tens of GB,
# and it deletes itself as it assembles.
data/*.building/

# Frames and their reductions, which are output, not source.
captures/
*.fits

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Cross-validation output: regenerated by `dotnet run` + the compare scripts, never edited.
# The numbers that matter are transcribed into ACCURACY.md.
validation/*.out
validation/**/exo_*.csv
validation/**/.skyfield-data/
validation/**/*.png

# Research records: your results, not source. Export them deliberately.
# Anchored to the root: a bare 'research/' also matched Engine/Research, which is source.
/research/
__pycache__/
